{"session_id":"2026-09-22_cms-ingestion-and-plagiarism-modernization","date":"2026-09-22T01:45:00.000Z","task_summary":"Comprehensive modernization of CMS-V2 ingestion and integrity validation pipeline: Deprecated legacy parsers and 384-dim embeddings. Deployed PaddleOCR-VL (0.9B) FastAPI document parsing microservice with PyMuPDF fast-path (<3 GB RAM envelope, 5-page GC batches, /health and POST /api/v1/parse-document). Upgraded vector core to BAAI/bge-m3 1024-dim representations with 8192-token context length and sparse lexical term-salience weights. Implemented two-stage HybridSourceTracker (HST): Stage 1 coarse ANN candidate retrieval (top-50) via HNSW cosine metric in blue/green collection (cms_documents_v2) + Stage 2 exact Winnowing n-gram and sparse lexical re-ranking. Integrated calibrated composite score (0.50 Winnowing + 0.30 Dense + 0.20 Sparse) with manual review gate (>=0.75) and critical alert gate (Winnowing >=0.85). Created idempotent migration backfill script (migrate_vectors_bge_m3.py), centralized Node.js ocrExtractionService with degraded local fallback, and docker-compose-v2.yml. Passed all 7 modernization tests, 4/4 ocrExtraction.service tests, 6/6 submission.review-flow tests, 204/182 endpoint parity (UNMATCHED_COUNT=0), and 60/60 agentic validation checks.","task_category":"ingestion_and_plagiarism_engine_modernization","skills_written":[],"skills_patched":["senior-backend","verification-loop","continual-learning"]}
